# The GCC whose -fanalyzer tools/gcc-analyzer/run.sh gates on (ticket sca-round3/07).
# One file that run.sh, the docs and CI all read, so the version is stated once.
#
# The analyzer's findings change between GCC releases (GCC 14's handles C considerably
# better than 13's), so a finding count means nothing without the compiler that produced
# it. The zero in docs/static-analysis.md was measured with exactly this build.
#
# GCC_MAJOR is what run.sh enforces locally. GCC_PACKAGE is the Ubuntu 24.04 package CI
# runs, at exactly GCC_PACKAGE_VERSION: the ubuntu-24.04 runner image ships it, and the
# devcontainer (same Ubuntu) has the same. CI does not install it (the archive keeps only
# the latest -updates build of a package, so an apt pin would fail rather than hold);
# run.sh --exact refuses any other version instead. When a runner image moves gcc-13
# forward, that failure is the signal to re-run the analyzer, triage what changed, and
# re-pin here in the same change.
GCC_MAJOR=13
GCC_PACKAGE=gcc-13
GCC_PACKAGE_VERSION=13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1
